MCP = Model Context Protocol

MCP is an open protocol for connecting AI applications/agents with external tools, resources and context through standardized interfaces.

Think of it as a common way for AI applications to discover and interact with capabilities provided by external systems.

Conceptually:

AI Agent
   ↓
MCP Client
   ↓
MCP Server
   ↓
Tools / Resources

Example:

An agent could interact with:

GitHub
Database
Files
CRM
Internal APIs

through MCP-compatible servers.
